  id: Scene07_FAQ_3
  speaker: WATTSON
  text: The batteries of 1826 faded as they worked, so the push kept changing during
    a measurement. A copper-bismuth junction, with one end in steam and the other
    in ice, gave a small but steady potential difference. Steady conditions, reliable
    readings.
